WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.401
James, David, gentlemen,
congratulations.

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:04.237
You are now moving
into the final round of

00:00:04.303 --> 00:00:06.005
this super-sized competition.

00:00:06.071 --> 00:00:07.807
But in this final
round, gentlemen,

00:00:07.873 --> 00:00:09.408
you'll be building
the largest weapon

00:00:09.508 --> 00:00:13.245
we have ever asked smiths to
make in Forged in Fire history.

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:15.581
Bladesmiths, in
the next four days,

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.150
you will be building this.

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:24.857
The nine foot long
Friauler Speiss.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.425
[laughter]

00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:29.361
The Friauler Speiss dates back
to 16th century northern Italy.

00:00:29.461 --> 00:00:32.798
The massive pole arm features
a 37 inch long central blade

00:00:32.865 --> 00:00:34.500
with two curved side blades.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:37.703
The shaft can measure up
to six feet long, perfect

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:41.941
for delivering lethal thrusts
and slashes upon enemy cavalry.

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:45.678
Over time, this enormous weapon
took on a more ceremonial role,

00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:49.248
and at its longest,
spanned more than 10 feet.

00:00:49.348 --> 00:00:50.616
Today, the Friauler
Speiss can be

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:53.018
seen on display at the
Metropolitan Museum of Art

00:00:53.118 --> 00:00:53.986
in New York City.

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:54.987
So good luck.

00:00:55.087 --> 00:00:56.189
You're going to need it.

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:57.524
We will see you
guys in four days.

00:01:01.193 --> 00:01:02.796 line:14%
My name is David Warner.

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:04.730 line:14%
I'm 37 years old.

00:01:04.797 --> 00:01:07.232 line:14%
I'm from Kirkwood, Missouri.

00:01:07.332 --> 00:01:10.402
I have twins, boy and a girl.

00:01:10.469 --> 00:01:14.106
And I would say that raising
twins has prepared me really

00:01:14.206 --> 00:01:16.909
well for this
competition, because I can

00:01:16.975 --> 00:01:18.677
deal with stressful situations.

00:01:18.744 --> 00:01:22.682
I'm kind of nervous about making
something that's this size

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:25.017
and then to put a spear
socket at the end of it.

00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:27.086
That's also a challenge.

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.289
And then get it to
attach to the socket.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:31.858
It's going to be a
pacing challenge.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.759
I need to start
shaping the handle.

00:01:33.859 --> 00:01:38.197
I've made some spears before,
but nothing quite like this.

00:01:38.263 --> 00:01:39.865
So I need to make sure
that the handle will

00:01:39.965 --> 00:01:41.433
actually fit inside the socket.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:44.070
I've got to make sure that
there's a pretty precise fit.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:48.308
So I think what I'm going
to do is heat up this guy

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:51.711
and try and use that heat to
press this in the post-Speiss

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:55.715
around there to get a
nice seal on that shaft.

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:57.082
That's what I was going for.

00:01:57.149 --> 00:01:59.418
Yesterday, I got
the blades quenched.

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:04.156
I just need to assemble
everything and sharpen it.

00:02:04.256 --> 00:02:05.692
I think this blade
has got a pretty good

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:07.794
shot of bringing home $10,000.

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:08.862
Who's hungry?

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:13.933 line:14%
My name is James Dean--

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.301 line:14%
like the actor.

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:17.603
I was a professional
chef for 25 years.

00:02:17.703 --> 00:02:20.173
The forge environment is
much like the kitchen.

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:22.708
It is hot, it is
angry, it is dirty.

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.977
But I get to create
something beautiful.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.044
You just don't eat it.

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:27.747
You can, it's just
not nutritious

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:28.815
and you might break a teeth.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:34.754
By the end of today, I
hope to accomplish stacking

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:38.224
up 230 layers of Damascus.

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:42.695
I want to do something to kind
of really elevate my build.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:47.600
First thing I'm going to do
is cut in my little Speiss.

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:50.803
Now that the pikes are
shaped, you got to quench.

00:02:50.903 --> 00:02:55.074
For something this big,
there's chances it might warp.

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.309
Push!

00:02:59.011 --> 00:03:01.013
It's got a little bit warped.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.515
It did take a little
bit of a warp,

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:05.150
but nothing that's not
within grinder range.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:06.920
The blade is hard.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.487
I'm super pumped.

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:10.590
So I'm going to try
grinding it out.

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:18.097
In the process of trying
to straighten my blade,

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:20.567
I ended up shattering it.

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:21.701
This is day four.

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:26.005
I have no time left,
but I'm starting over.

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.740
Being that I only
have nine hours,

00:03:27.806 --> 00:03:30.375
I have to try to make the
build out of a model steel

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:32.412
just so I can get
it done in time.

00:03:36.782 --> 00:03:42.421
Since my time is short, I have
to rush the heat treatment.

00:03:42.521 --> 00:03:44.190
I really didn't
get much of a warm.

00:03:44.256 --> 00:03:45.424
I feel pretty good about this.

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:46.425
I had a huge comeback.

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:48.160
I'm the comeback kid.

00:03:48.227 --> 00:03:50.563
Who builds the biggest
weapon in "Forged

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:54.667
in Fire" history in nine
hours on the last day?

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:55.868
I dare you.

00:03:55.935 --> 00:04:01.240
Bladesmiths, welcome
to the dynamic kill test.

00:04:01.306 --> 00:04:03.675
But as massive as
your weapons are,

00:04:03.742 --> 00:04:05.577
it's not as massive
as my disappointment

00:04:05.644 --> 00:04:08.381
that I can't wield them today
because of my injury here.

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:11.150
But I leave you in capable
hands with a man of the plan

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:14.386
who'll be my hand, Dave Baker.

00:04:14.453 --> 00:04:16.489
David, you're up first.
Are you ready for this?

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:17.256
Yes I am.

00:04:17.356 --> 00:04:20.326
All right, let's do this.

00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:22.929
[music playing]

00:04:57.563 --> 00:05:01.067
So David, when you're
swinging a nine foot weapon,

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:02.568
it's pretty wild.

00:05:02.634 --> 00:05:05.604
It went into the pig with
no resistance whatsoever.

00:05:05.671 --> 00:05:08.674
The blade, it's all still
true, it's all still sharp.

00:05:08.774 --> 00:05:09.609
Nicely done.

00:05:09.675 --> 00:05:11.243
Doug, you got anything to add?

00:05:11.343 --> 00:05:15.915
Your weapon will kill.

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:17.249
All right James, you ready?

00:05:17.349 --> 00:05:19.319
Slice, dice, and bacon.

00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:25.692
[music playing]

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:33.066
[grunting]

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:01.460
All right, James,
right off, it

00:06:01.526 --> 00:06:02.762
did what it's supposed to do.

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:04.796
But there are some
spots that are dull.

00:06:04.863 --> 00:06:06.833
Like I can literally
rub my finger on it.

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:10.636
And we've picked up a
significant bend in the blade.

00:06:10.736 --> 00:06:13.305
But having said that, Doug--

00:06:13.372 --> 00:06:16.275
Your weapon, sir, will kill.

00:06:16.342 --> 00:06:17.510
Thank you.

00:06:21.047 --> 00:06:25.017
Bladesmiths, welcome to
the dynamic strength test.

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:28.587
To test the strength and overall
construction of your weapons,

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:32.191
I will be pushing on these
poles, snapping all 10 of them,

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:34.527
and then piercing
these steel drums.

00:06:34.594 --> 00:06:35.961
Dave, you're up first.
You ready?

00:06:36.028 --> 00:06:36.962
Yes I am.

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:39.331
All right.

00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:42.635
[music playing]

00:07:28.113 --> 00:07:29.015
All right, David.

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:30.916
Well, your blade held up great.

00:07:31.016 --> 00:07:33.585
In piercing the drums,
took some serious flex,

00:07:33.685 --> 00:07:34.953
but came right back to true.

00:07:35.054 --> 00:07:37.756
The side blades here, they
penetrated that barrel,

00:07:37.857 --> 00:07:39.424
and I don't even
see any indication

00:07:39.491 --> 00:07:40.659
that they were in there.

00:07:40.726 --> 00:07:42.161
All in all, I think
you did a great job,

00:07:42.227 --> 00:07:44.363
and your weapon held up great.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:45.798
Thank you.

00:07:45.865 --> 00:07:47.200
All right, James.
You're up, man.

00:07:47.266 --> 00:07:49.034
You ready?
- Pick it up, fire it up.

00:07:49.101 --> 00:07:50.102
All right.

00:07:52.605 --> 00:07:55.808
[music playing]

00:08:37.582 --> 00:08:38.651
All right, James.

00:08:38.717 --> 00:08:40.886
It looks like your
tip held up fine.

00:08:40.953 --> 00:08:44.823
But your blade took a
pretty significant warp.

00:08:44.924 --> 00:08:46.726
It's kind of doing
an S-curve now.

00:08:46.826 --> 00:08:48.427
But all in all, it
held up pretty good.

00:08:48.494 --> 00:08:49.428
Nice job.

00:08:49.495 --> 00:08:50.763
Thank you.

00:08:53.265 --> 00:08:55.601
Well, bladesmiths, this has
been a hell of a competition

00:08:55.668 --> 00:08:57.035
from the beginning.

00:08:57.102 --> 00:08:58.704
But at the end of this
competition, only one of you

00:08:58.771 --> 00:09:01.106
can come out on top, earning
the check for $10,000

00:09:01.173 --> 00:09:03.108
and the title of Forged
in Fire champion.

00:09:03.175 --> 00:09:09.481
Today's Forged in Fire
champion is David.

00:09:09.582 --> 00:09:10.949
Congratulations.

00:09:11.016 --> 00:09:12.684
Well, James, you're
a talented smith.

00:09:12.784 --> 00:09:13.985
You've been talented all the
way through this competition.

00:09:14.052 --> 00:09:15.454
We want to say thank
you for coming out,

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:16.689
but your time here has ended.

00:09:16.756 --> 00:09:18.223
I'm going to have
to ask you to please

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:19.324
step off the forge floor.
- Thanks for the opportunity.

00:09:19.391 --> 00:09:20.326
Thank you.

00:09:20.392 --> 00:09:21.627
Thank you, James.

00:09:21.694 --> 00:09:24.029
I feel devastated
after the test.

00:09:24.129 --> 00:09:25.197
I really wanted to win.

00:09:25.264 --> 00:09:27.466
But, I mean, I made the
biggest blade in Forged

00:09:27.532 --> 00:09:29.168
in Fire history in nine hours.

00:09:29.268 --> 00:09:32.070
And I'm proud of it.

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:35.073
David, that makes you a
Forged in Fire champion, man.

00:09:35.173 --> 00:09:37.509
You're going to be getting
a check for $10,000.

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:38.877
Very well done.

00:09:38.944 --> 00:09:39.744
Thank you.

00:09:39.845 --> 00:09:42.280
I'm still kind
of just processing

00:09:42.347 --> 00:09:44.116
that that just happened.

00:09:44.216 --> 00:09:48.387
A big chunk of this $10,000
is going to go toward getting

00:09:48.487 --> 00:09:50.322
my kids their education.

00:09:50.422 --> 00:09:52.024
I'm just excited.

00:09:52.091 --> 00:09:55.127
[music playing]

